                'summary' => 'Kisah Nyi Endit, seorang janda kaya namun serakah yang menghina seorang pengemis tua, hingga desanya tenggelam menjadi danau Situ Bagendit sebagai hukuman atas ketamakannya.',
                'minutes' => 7,
                'xp' => 25,
                'content' => "A long time ago, in a village in West Java, there lived a very rich woman named Nyi Endit. She had a big house, many rice fields, and more gold than anyone else in the village. But Nyi Endit was not a kind woman. She was very **greedy**, and she never wanted to share her money with anyone.\n\nThe poor people in the village often needed help. Sometimes their rice fields failed, and their families were hungry. They asked Nyi Endit for a little rice or a little money. But she always said no. She shouted at them and told them to go away. She loved her gold more than she loved other people.\n\nOne day, the village had a big celebration. Everyone came together to eat, sing, and dance. In the middle of the party, a strange old beggar appeared. His clothes were dirty and torn, and he looked very hungry. He walked up to Nyi Endit and politely asked for some food.\n\nNyi Endit looked at the poor old man with disgust. Instead of giving him food, she laughed at him in front of everyone. She called him dirty and useless and told the guards to chase him away from her party. The old beggar did not get angry. He simply turned and walked to the edge of the village.\n\nThere, the old man pushed a small wooden stick into the ground. He said that only a truly innocent person could pull it out again. Many strong men from the village tried, but the stick would not move. Then a poor orphan boy walked up and touched it gently, and the stick came out easily, all by itself.\n\nThe moment the stick was pulled out, water began to **gush** from the hole in the ground. It did not stop. It grew bigger and bigger, faster and faster, until the whole village was flooding. The old beggar had disappeared, but people understood that he had supernatural powers, and that this flood was punishment for Nyi Endit's cruelty.\n\nThe water covered Nyi Endit's entire house and all her gold, and she **drowned** along with her riches. The flood formed a wide, deep lake where the village used to be. People named the new lake **Situ Bagendit**, after the greedy woman who once lived there. Even today, parents in West Java tell this story to teach their children to be generous and kind to those in need.",
                'translated_content' => "Dahulu kala, di sebuah desa di Jawa Barat, hiduplah seorang wanita yang sangat kaya bernama Nyi Endit. Ia punya rumah besar, banyak sawah, dan lebih banyak emas daripada siapa pun di desa itu. Tetapi Nyi Endit bukan wanita yang baik hati. Ia sangat tamak, dan ia tidak pernah mau membagikan uangnya kepada siapa pun.\n\nOrang-orang miskin di desa itu sering membutuhkan bantuan. Kadang-kadang sawah mereka gagal panen, dan keluarga mereka kelaparan. Mereka meminta sedikit beras atau sedikit uang kepada Nyi Endit. Tetapi ia selalu menolak. Ia membentak mereka dan menyuruh mereka pergi. Ia lebih mencintai emasnya daripada mencintai orang lain.\n\nSuatu hari, desa itu mengadakan sebuah perayaan besar. Semua orang berkumpul untuk makan, bernyanyi, dan menari. Di tengah pesta itu, seorang pengemis tua yang aneh muncul. Pakaiannya kotor dan compang-camping, dan ia terlihat sangat lapar. Ia berjalan mendekati Nyi Endit dan dengan sopan meminta sedikit makanan.\n\nNyi Endit memandang pria tua miskin itu dengan jijik. Alih-alih memberinya makanan, ia menertawakannya di depan semua orang. Ia menyebutnya kotor dan tidak berguna, lalu menyuruh penjaganya mengusirnya dari pestanya. Pengemis tua itu tidak marah. Ia hanya berbalik dan berjalan menuju pinggir desa.\n\nDi sana, pria tua itu menancapkan sebatang kayu kecil ke tanah. Ia berkata bahwa hanya orang yang benar-benar tulus yang bisa mencabutnya kembali. Banyak pria kuat dari desa itu mencoba, tetapi kayu itu tidak bergerak sama sekali. Kemudian seorang anak yatim piatu miskin datang dan menyentuhnya dengan lembut, dan kayu itu tercabut dengan mudah, dengan sendirinya.\n\nBegitu kayu itu tercabut, air mulai menyembur dari lubang di tanah. Air itu tidak berhenti. Semakin lama semakin besar, semakin cepat, hingga seluruh desa terendam banjir. Pengemis tua itu telah menghilang, tetapi orang-orang mengerti bahwa ia memiliki kekuatan gaib, dan bahwa banjir ini adalah hukuman atas kekejaman Nyi Endit.\n\nAir itu menutupi seluruh rumah Nyi Endit dan semua emasnya, dan ia tenggelam bersama harta bendanya. Banjir itu membentuk sebuah danau yang luas dan dalam di tempat desa itu dulu berada. Orang-orang menamai danau baru itu Situ Bagendit, dari nama wanita tamak yang dulu tinggal di sana. Hingga hari ini, orang tua di Jawa Barat menceritakan kisah ini untuk mengajarkan anak-anak mereka agar murah hati dan baik kepada mereka yang membutuhkan.",
