            [
                'title' => 'Kancil and the Crocodiles',
                'level' => 'Beginner',
                'summary' => 'Kisah Kancil yang cerdik menipu sekawanan buaya agar berbaris di sungai, sehingga ia bisa melompati punggung mereka untuk mencapai kebun buah di seberang.',
                'minutes' => 6,
                'xp' => 25,
                'content' => "In the forest, there lived a small and clever mouse-deer named **Kancil**. One hot day, Kancil felt very hungry. He looked across the wide river and saw a garden full of ripe, juicy fruit on the other side. He wanted to eat the fruit very much, but he had one big problem: the river was full of hungry crocodiles.\n\nThe crocodiles lived in the water, and they always waited for animals to swim by so they could eat them. Kancil knew he could not swim across safely. So he sat by the river and thought hard. After a while, a clever idea came into his mind.\n\nKancil walked to the edge of the water and called out loudly to the crocodiles. He said, \"Hello, friends! I have important news from the king! The king wants to know exactly how many crocodiles live in this river. He is sending gifts of meat to every crocodile, but first, he needs a count.\"\n\nThe crocodiles were very excited to hear about gifts of meat. They swam close to Kancil, all talking at once. Kancil said, \"Please line up in a row across the river, from this side to the other side. Then I will hop along your backs and count each one of you.\" The crocodiles quickly agreed and lined up in a long, straight row.\n\nKancil began to hop, one crocodile back to the next, counting out loud: \"One, two, three...\" The crocodiles stayed very still, waiting patiently for their gifts. But Kancil was not really counting, he was using their backs like stepping stones to cross the river! When he reached the very last crocodile, he gave a big jump and landed safely on the other side.\n\nThe crocodiles finally understood that they had been **tricked**, but it was too late. Kancil was already standing in the fruit garden, laughing happily. He picked the sweetest fruit and ate until he was full, proud that his clever brain had helped him **outsmart** the dangerous crocodiles once again.",
                'translated_content' => "Di hutan, hiduplah seekor kancil kecil yang cerdik bernama Kancil. Suatu hari yang panas, Kancil merasa sangat lapar. Ia melihat ke seberang sungai yang lebar dan melihat sebuah kebun penuh buah yang matang dan segar di seberang sana. Ia sangat ingin memakan buah-buahan itu, tetapi ia punya satu masalah besar: sungai itu penuh dengan buaya-buaya yang lapar.\n\nBuaya-buaya itu tinggal di dalam air, dan mereka selalu menunggu hewan-hewan yang berenang lewat agar bisa memakannya. Kancil tahu ia tidak bisa berenang menyeberang dengan aman. Jadi ia duduk di tepi sungai dan berpikir keras. Setelah beberapa saat, sebuah ide cerdik muncul di kepalanya.\n\nKancil berjalan ke tepi air dan berteriak lantang kepada para buaya. Ia berkata, \"Halo, teman-teman! Aku punya kabar penting dari raja! Raja ingin tahu persis berapa banyak buaya yang tinggal di sungai ini. Ia akan mengirim hadiah daging untuk setiap buaya, tetapi pertama-tama, ia perlu menghitung kalian.\"\n\nPara buaya sangat senang mendengar tentang hadiah daging. Mereka berenang mendekati Kancil, semua berbicara sekaligus. Kancil berkata, \"Tolong berbaris dalam satu barisan melintasi sungai, dari sisi ini ke sisi seberang. Lalu aku akan melompat di punggung kalian dan menghitung kalian satu per satu.\" Para buaya segera setuju dan berbaris dalam satu barisan panjang dan lurus.\n\nKancil mulai melompat, dari punggung satu buaya ke buaya berikutnya, menghitung dengan keras: \"Satu, dua, tiga...\" Para buaya tetap diam, menunggu dengan sabar hadiah mereka. Tetapi Kancil sebenarnya tidak sedang menghitung, ia menggunakan punggung mereka seperti batu loncatan untuk menyeberangi sungai! Ketika ia sampai di buaya terakhir, ia melompat tinggi dan mendarat dengan selamat di seberang sungai.\n\nPara buaya akhirnya sadar bahwa mereka telah ditipu, tetapi sudah terlambat. Kancil sudah berdiri di kebun buah, tertawa bahagia. Ia memetik buah paling manis dan makan sampai kenyang, bangga karena otaknya yang cerdik telah membantunya mengecoh para buaya yang berbahaya itu sekali lagi.",
                'items' => [
                    ['term' => 'clever', 'reading' => null, 'romaji' => null, 'meaning' => 'cerdik, pintar', 'example' => null, 'example_meaning' => null, 'extra' => ['type' => 'glossary']],
                    ['term' => 'hungry', 'reading' => null, 'romaji' => null, 'meaning' => 'lapar', 'example' => null, 'example_meaning' => null, 'extra' => ['type' => 'glossary']],
